# DOCKER-USER policy, IPv6. Managed by bin/provision-host.sh and reconciled by
# agentic-postgres-docker-firewall.service after every docker.service start.
#
# Applied only when host.yaml configures an expected_public_ipv6. A half-applied
# IPv6 policy is worse than none: it looks like coverage in a review and leaves
# the actual path open, so provision-host.sh either applies this whole file or
# records that IPv6 is not configured.
#
# Identical in shape to the v4 policy, and identical in the detail that matters:
# --ctorigdstport rather than --dport, because DNAT has already rewritten the
# destination by the time a packet reaches FORWARD.
#
# Substituted by provision-host.sh:
#   __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__   resolved from host.yaml, or from the default route
#                          when public_interface is `auto`.

-i __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__ -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j RETURN

-i __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__ -p tcp -m conntrack --ctstate NEW --ctorigdstport 80 -j RETURN
-i __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__ -p tcp -m conntrack --ctstate NEW --ctorigdstport 443 -j RETURN

# ICMPv6 is not optional the way ICMP is on v4. Path MTU discovery and neighbour
# discovery both depend on it, and dropping it produces connections that
# complete and then hang on the first large response -- a failure that looks
# like an application problem for a long time before anyone suspects the
# firewall. Rate-limited rather than unrestricted.
#
# `10/sec`, not `10/second`. They mean the same thing to iptables, but iptables
# echoes the short form back from `-S`, so writing the long one makes the
# installed policy and the running policy differ as text while being identical
# in effect. The comparison that proves the kernel is running this file is
# exact, deliberately -- normalising spellings inside it would mean maintaining
# a table of iptables' preferences, and every entry in such a table is a
# difference the check has agreed in advance not to notice.
-i __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__ -p ipv6-icmp -m limit --limit 10/sec -j RETURN

-i __PUBLIC_INTERFACE__ -j DROP
